      <activity id="f082f3ab-ec73-5605-bacf-70574a98663b" activityNameId="87693287-5f35-5132-af73-77e317e552d7" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Window frame, wood, U=1.2 W/m2K, market mix, wall opening, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Window frame, wood, U=1.2 W/m2K, market mix, wall opening, at plant
The measures of the window are 1.75m (width) x 1.3m (height). The wall opening is 1.8 m2 (assumption width of frame 0.12m, 2/3 of frame are behind the wall opening). 1m2 (wall opening) of wooden window frame weighs 21.1kg.The bill of materials is based on data from 3 window producers.;
UUID: 246aca1f-5cb1-3396-8dac-8126859b40b3
Included are the materials for the production of a wooden window frame and an average surface treatment. Production losses, work materials, packaging materials, energy demand and the transport of the materials are also included.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at 4 window manufacturers in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_246aca1f-5cb1-3396-8dac-8126859b40b3.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
